        "original_id": "f01a1bc5-7323-5c3c-9c1b-00bd8370b9b7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ridley Scott, Elmer Clifton, D. W. Griffith, Joseph Henabery, Eric Garcia\n- Films: Alien, Blade Runner, Gladiator, The Martian, The Birth of a Nation, Intolerance, Matchstick Men, Swamp Woman\n- Roles: film director, producer, actor, mentor\n- Topics: film careers, collaborations, adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Ridley Scott was born on 30 November 1937 and is an English film director and producer.\n- Elmer Clifton collaborated with D. W. Griffith and appeared in The Birth of a Nation in 1915.\n- Elmer Clifton appeared in Intolerance in 1916.\n- Elmer Clifton gave up acting in 1917 to concentrate on behind-the-camera work, with D. W. Griffith and Joseph Henabery as his mentors.\n- Ridley Scott had a commercial breakthrough with Alien in 1979.\n- Ridley Scott directed Blade Runner in 1982.\n- Elmer Clifton directed the American film Swamp Woman in 1941.\n- Ridley Scott directed the British-American black comedy crime film Matchstick Men in 2003.\n- Matchstick Men was based on Eric Garcia's 2002 novel of the same name.\n- Gladiator, directed by Ridley Scott, won the Best Picture Oscar in 2000.\n- Ridley Scott directed The Martian in 2015.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
